# CORS origins

Edit the origin list in both of these places in the same change:

- `SecurityConfig.corsConfigurationSource`
- `WebConfig.addCorsMappings`

`SecurityConfig` must keep `.cors(Customizer.withDefaults())` and `OPTIONS /**` as `permitAll`. `WebConfig` alone does not cover secured routes.

Both lists use exact origins and `allowCredentials(true)`. Do not switch either list to `*`. `http://localhost:5173` and `http://127.0.0.1:5173` are different origins. Keep both.

```java
// BAD — updated in only one class, so the browser and Spring Security disagree
// WebConfig only
.allowedOrigins("https://new-preview.vercel.app")

// GOOD — same origin added in SecurityConfig and WebConfig
"http://localhost:5173",
"http://127.0.0.1:5173",
"https://booking-app-frontend-kappa.vercel.app",
"https://new-preview.vercel.app"
```

A `401` on `POST /Public/LoginUser` from a bad `jwtToken` cookie is `JwtFilter`, not a missing CORS origin.
